                <pb facs="0639" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-09T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1920—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 9—1:49 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>166. The following telegram has been received from Stevens: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Harbin, July 6, 10 p.m. Orders are issued for the evacuation Japanese
                            troops from the Trans-Baikal region. Destination is unknown. At their
                            request we are sending 2000 box and 200 passenger cars for the
                            movement.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
